"""black_strand story pass (22 Nov 2026), to docs/quest_writing_standard.md. Where the giver's speech sat in the accept
line and the journal showed a summary or narration, the speech is now the description and the accept line a new short
beat; the rest were written fresh. Turn-ins untouched."""

STORY = {
    'bst_long_way_down': (
        "You'll want the town. There's an inn, and you look like you could use one.\n\nTake this token to Gate-Captain Yrsa. It tells her I've seen you and you came down the stair, not up out of the sand. She likes to know.\n\nThe slag road starts right here and runs south-east. Stay on it and follow the braziers. The gate's at the end, between the two watchtowers.",
        "Keep the token dry. Yrsa won't take a soggy one, and she'll make you walk back for another.",
    ),
    'bst_clear_the_slag_road': (
        "You walked in on the slag road, so you'll have seen what's on it.\n\nThe Blacksand Scorpions bury themselves in the black sand beside the paving and the Strand Bats come down off the roof at anything carrying a lamp. We lose a carter to them every couple of months.\n\nThey're thickest out on the Ash Dunes, north-west of the gate, the way you came. Kill what you find near the road. I'd do it myself but I'm not allowed off this gate.",
        "Shutter your lamp while you walk out there. It'll keep the bats off you until you're ready for them.",
    ),
    'bst_keep_them_lit': (
        "See the braziers? The hive won't come past them. I don't know why and I don't much care, as long as they stay lit.\n\nThey burn basilisk fat. Coal smokes too much in a cave and lamp oil comes down a rope, so it's fat or nothing. We're nearly out.\n\nThe Ashdune Basilisks are out on the Ash Dunes, north-west of the gate. Don't look them in the eye for long. Bring me the fat and I'll render it tonight.",
        "Bring it in a sack, not your pockets. You'll never get the smell out.",
    ),
    'bst_sign_the_board': (
        "Some of mine signed out to dig dark iron in the sand, out on the Ash Dunes. That was five shifts ago and none of them has signed back in.\n\nI've a fair idea what happened. The basilisks out there turn a body to stone if it stands still long enough, and miners stand still a lot.\n\nThe sand diggings are north-west of the gate, off the south side of the slag road. Go and look. If I'm right, the Ashdune Basilisks will have what's left. Bring me the picks. Each one has a name on the haft and I need to know which names.",
        "Read me the names off the hafts when you're back. I'd rather hear them than look.",
    ),
    'bst_bats_in_the_flue': (
        "The furnace has been drawing badly all week. I went up the flue with a lamp and it's full of bats.\n\nThe flue comes out through the rock onto the Ash Dunes, north-west of the gate. It's warm, so they roost in it. Every time I clear them out, more come in from the dunes.\n\nThin out the Strand Bats out there and I'll have a chance of keeping it clear. Garrun's blaming my shovelling and I'd like him to stop.",
        "If you see Garrun on your way out, don't tell him I asked.",
    ),
    'bst_forgemasters_test': (
        "Anybody can swing a pick. I want to see what you do with what comes out.\n\nThere's dark iron ore in the sand all over the Strand, and in our own rock if Kelda lets you down the head. Mine some and smelt it into bars. You'll need the skill for it. If you haven't got it yet, come back when you have.\n\nDark iron's fussy. Too cold and it won't flow, too hot and it goes brittle. Bring me the bars and I'll tell you which you did.",
        "Don't rush the bars. I'll know if you did.",
    ),
    'bst_a_keg_for_the_stair': (
        "Hervi's been on the stair post for three weeks without relief. Nobody's sent him anything but bread.\n\nTake him this keg, would you? He's at the Bottom Step, at the far north-west end of the slag road, where you came down. It's heavy but it's a straight road.\n\nTell him it's from Brenna and he still owes me for the last one.",
        "Roll it if your arms give out. The road's flat enough.",
    ),
    'bst_tide_marks': (
        "Can I ask you something? You'll be walking across the dunes anyway.\n\nThere are lines on the cavern walls out there, high up. Pale bands, dead level, one above another. I think they're tide marks. If they are, they should be at the same height on both sides of the cavern.\n\nI can't get to the far wall. There's too much out there that wants to eat me. The Ash Dunes are just south-east of here. Have a look at the west wall and then the east one, and tell me whether the lines match.",
        "Look closely at both walls, because if the lines match, I've been right all along.",
    ),
    'bst_black_sand': (
        "The sand's bothering me. Beach sand is pale. This is black and it's heavy, and the dwarves dig iron out of it.\n\nI'd like to see a fresh cut, somewhere it's been dug deep. The miners have a diggings on the Ash Dunes, south-east of here on the south side of the slag road. Go and look at how the sand lies in the sides of the pit.\n\nThe Blacksand Scorpions nest in the loose spoil round it. You'll have to clear them before you can see anything.",
        "Clear the scorpions first. I'd rather you came back to tell me about it.",
    ),
    'bst_whose_shore': (
        "A carter brought me a shell last month. It had a hole drilled in it, clean through, and a pattern scratched round the hole. Shells don't grow like that. Somebody made it.\n\nHe got it out of a Blindwater Lurker. They swallow anything on the bottom and it sits in the gut for years.\n\nThe Lurkers are at the Last Water. Go out of the gate and south, past the big rock, until you reach the lake. If you find any more shells like it, I want them.",
        'Gut them over a cloth so nothing small gets lost in the sand.',
    ),
    'bst_standing_stones': (
        "If they wore shells, they'll have left more than shells.\n\nThe carters talk about three stones. They call them the Old Men. Two are in the Lantern Wood and one's by the Last Water. I'd always assumed they were stalagmites. Now I'm not so sure.\n\nThe Lantern Wood is south-west of the gate. One stone is at its far west end and one at its north edge. The third is on the west shore of the Last Water, south of the gate. Go and look at each of them closely. I want to know if they've been shaped.",
        'Run your hand along each one. Tool marks feel different from water.',
    ),
    'bst_two_notebooks': (
        "Hervi tells me there's a topside woman camped at the Bottom Step who measures the walls. He thinks she's cracked. I think she might be asking the same thing I am.\n\nI can't leave the town. The Thane's made that clear. So would you take her my notes? The shells, the stones, all of it.\n\nThe Bottom Step is at the far north-west end of the slag road. I don't know her name. She'll be the only person there who isn't a dwarf.",
        "Tell her I'd like her thoughts back, when she's had time to read them.",
    ),
    'bst_young_caps': (
        "I'm down to my last jar of caps and I've orders to fill.\n\nI need young ones, picked before they open. Once they open the good part's gone into the air. The trouble is the young caps walk about. We call them Lantern Sporelings, and they don't like being picked.\n\nThe Lantern Wood is south-west of the gate. You'll see the glow well before you get there. Kill the Sporelings and cut the caps off before they open.",
        'Cut them close to the stalk, and keep them out of the light on the way back.',
    ),
    'bst_trampler_gills': (
        "Half the furnace crew has a cough that won't shift. It's the smoke. I can make something for it, but I need gills from the big mushrooms.\n\nGloomcap Tramplers, we call them. They're slow, but they're the size of a cart and they'll walk straight over you. They're in the Lantern Wood, south-west of the gate, further in than the Sporelings.\n\nCut the gills from under the cap. Wear something over your mouth while you do it.",
        "Get out of their way first and cut second. They don't stop for anyone.",
    ),
    'bst_the_last_water': (
        "There's a lake south of here. It's the only standing water left in this whole cavern, so we call it the Last Water.\n\nI need to know if it's rising or falling. If it's falling, the rock above us is drying out and it'll crack. If it's rising, something's leaking in from above, and that's worse.\n\nGo out of the gate and south. Look at the shoreline on the north side and then on the south. Wet rock above the waterline means it's dropped. The Blindwater Lurkers will come at you the moment you're near the edge, so deal with them first.",
        "Check both shores before you come back. One side alone won't tell me much.",
    ),
    'bst_water_for_the_quench': (
        "Our well water's too soft. Dark iron quenched in it comes out with a skin like an eggshell.\n\nThe Last Water's hard and bitter and very cold, and blades quenched in it hold an edge twice as long. I'd send an apprentice with buckets, but the Blindwater Lurkers take apprentices.\n\nThe Lurkers carry water in a bladder under the jaw. Kill them and bring me the bladders, full. The lake's south of the gate.",
        "Keep the bladders full and the seals tight. A dry one's no use to me.",
    ),
    'bst_the_lights_go_out': (
        "The east side of the wood's gone dark. I noticed when I was out for caps. A whole stretch that used to glow has nothing growing in it now.\n\nMushrooms don't just stop. Something's taking them.\n\nGo and look, would you? The Lantern Wood is south-west of the gate, and the dark part is on its east side, nearest the lake. If it's what I think it is, you'll find Hive Swarmers there, so kill them.",
        'Look before you fight. I need to know what you saw.',
    ),
    'bst_names_in_the_book': (
        "You've heard people here go quiet about the old diggings. I'll tell you why, since nobody else will.\n\nAsk me what you like. Then go and see the place for yourself. It's north-east of the gate, where the slag road ends. You'll know it by the broken gate arch. Don't go in further than that unless you mean to fight.",
        "Stop at the arch. You'll see enough from there to understand.",
    ),
    'bst_the_old_diggings': (
        "I'll say this plainly. The people in the old diggings were ours, and I don't enjoy this.\n\nBut they've started raiding the slag road. Two carts last month, and a carter with his arm broken. They've no forge and no stores, so they take ours.\n\nThe Castout Diggings are north-east of the gate, at the end of the road. Go up there and push them back. The Castout Diggers and the Cutthroats are the ones doing the raiding. Leave anyone who doesn't raise a hand to you.",
        "Bring me a count of how many you saw up there, fighting or not. All I've got now is guesses.",
    ),
    'bst_brannocs_shift': (
        "You've been in and out of that gate. You'll have heard their side. I've had three years in the old diggings to think about mine.\n\nI'd like you to hear mine. It won't take long. After that there's something I need, and I can't get it myself.\n\nEvery miner on my shift kept a tally stick. It's notched for each cart, and it's branded with the gallery you were working. The Diggers still carry theirs. They're up in the Castout Diggings, north-east of here. They won't hand them over. Most of them think I'm a traitor for sitting this close to the gate.",
        "Take them however you have to, but don't tell them I sent you.",
    ),
    'bst_weights_still_true': (
        "Aldis keeps the weigh-books. Every cart that came out of every gallery is written down in them, with the name of whoever filled it.\n\nIf she sets these sticks against her books, she can show where each of us was working that shift. That's all I want. I'm not asking to be forgiven.\n\nShe's at the vault in the north-east corner of the town. Tell her they came from me.",
        "Hand her the bundle as it is. I've tied it in shift order.",
    ),
    'bst_the_thanes_answer': (
        "Aldis has shown me her books. I've spent all night with them.\n\nThree years ago, the day the ground shook, a gallery came down and killed eleven of my people.\n\nI put out forty people for what nine of them did. I did it because nobody would give me a name, and I took that for guilt. It was fear. I should have known the difference.\n\nThey can come home, all of them who want to. But Durn won't let them. He was Foreman of that shift, he ordered them into a gallery he'd been told was unsafe, and he's run the old diggings ever since. Anyone who tries to leave, he kills.\n\nHe's in the Castout Diggings, north-east of the gate. I'm not asking you to bring him back.",
        "When it's done, come and tell me yourself rather than sending word through the guards.",
    ),
    'bst_the_shrine_fire': (
        "When they were put out, some of them took fire from this bowl with them. I let them. It seemed wrong to send people into the dark without it.\n\nI shouldn't have. The ones we call Slagcallers have done something to it. They feed it things that aren't coal, and it burns the wrong colour now.\n\nIt's still our fire. I want it back before they do worse with it. The Slagcallers are in the Castout Diggings, north-east of the gate. They each carry some of it in a clay pot.",
        'Keep the pots upright, or that fire will find something of yours to burn.',
    ),
    'bst_listening_at_the_wall': (
        "I can hear digging through the wall. I've heard it every night this month, and it's getting closer. They never dug this way before the change.\n\nIt's the big ones, the Sandburrowers. They tunnel, and the rest of the hive follows down the tunnel after them.\n\nThe Chitin Reach is south-east of the gate. I want to know how far north they've dug. Look along the north edge of the Reach, the side nearest the town, at the west end and the east end. Kill any Hive Sandburrowers you find working there.",
        "Put your ear to the ground at both ends. You'll hear them before you see them.",
    ),
    'bst_a_charge_down_the_hole': (
        "Rurik says they're tunnelling at the wall. I've got just the thing.\n\nThese are slow charges. You set one at the mouth of a burrow, light the fuse and walk away. Don't run, because it looks bad and you've plenty of time.\n\nThere are three big burrows in the Chitin Reach, south-east of the gate. One's on the west side, one's up at the north and one's down at the south. Drop a charge at each. The hive won't thank you, so expect company.",
        "Keep the charges away from your lamp on the way out. I'd like the burrows to go up, not you.",
    ),
    'bst_amber_for_runes': (
        "I fill my runes with silver. It works, but it's soft and it wears out.\n\nThe hive makes a resin that sets clear and hard as glass. If I can inlay a rune with that, it should last as long as the plate does. I've only ever had a thumb's worth to try.\n\nThe Resinspitters make it. They're in the Chitin Reach, south-east of the gate. They'll spit it at you, which is unpleasant, but what I need is the clear stuff they carry inside.",
        "Wipe off the spit before you bring it in. That part's no good to me.",
    ),
    'bst_reaver_plate': (
        "One of the gate guards came back with a Reaver's back-plate strapped on as a shield. It turned a pick. I tried it myself.\n\nIt's lighter than dark iron and nearly as hard. I want to know if it can be riveted. If it can, I can make armour for the carters that they'll actually wear.\n\nThe Hive Reavers are in the Chitin Reach, south-east of the gate. They're the ones that walk upright. I need the back-plates whole, so try not to crack them.",
        "Go for the joints, not the back, or you'll ruin the plate I want.",
    ),
    'bst_toward_the_wood': (
        "Sigrun says the hive's in her wood. Rurik says it's under my wall. They're both right, and I haven't the guards to hold both.\n\nSo I'm not going to hold either. I want the hive hurt badly enough at home that it pulls its raiders back.\n\nGo into the Chitin Reach, south-east of the gate, and kill Reavers and Swarmers until they stop coming out to meet you. Then come and tell me how deep the place goes.",
        'Count how many tunnels you pass on the way in. I want a number.',
    ),
    'bst_the_royal_cell': (
        "Yrsa's told me. There's a queen.\n\nWe've lived beside that hive since we opened the gate. We burned its tunnels and it took our carters, and both sides could bear that. A hive that's farming and digging at my wall is a different matter. It means to grow.\n\nIt stops growing if the queen dies. The Royal Cell is at the far south-east corner of the cavern, through the back of the Chitin Reach. Her name, if the old tablets are right, is Zil'kesh.\n\nI can't spare guards for this. I'm asking you.",
        "Go when you're ready and not a day before. I'd rather wait than lose you.",
    ),
    'bst_the_roof_report': (
        "I've told the Thane the lake's falling and the roof's drying. He asked me how long we have. I couldn't tell him.\n\nI can hear the roof from underneath. I can't see the top of it. Somebody up there must be able to.\n\nYou came down through the desert. Is there anyone up there who measures the ground? If there is, take them these. They're my soundings, three years of them, from the day the ground shook to now.\n\nThe only way up is the way you came: the stair at the Bottom Step, through the dry caves, and up one of the pits. Fourth Peg is the camp in the north-east of the Abyssal Sands.",
        "Give her all three years. She'll want the early pages most.",
    ),
    'bst_what_peska_sent_back': (
        "Right, I've put her numbers and mine together.\n\nIt isn't good, but it's better than not knowing. The roof over that town will stand for about forty years if nothing changes. If somebody kills what's eating the pillars and keeps killing it, it'll stand a good deal longer.\n\nTake this to whoever runs the place. Tell them I'll send my crew down to shore the worst pillars if they'll send miners up to help. They know rock better than we do.\n\nBack the way you came: down a pit, through the Dry Deep to its east end, and down the stair. Onyxhollow's gate is at the end of the slag road.",
        "Tell the Thane I'm offering my own crew, so he knows I mean it.",
    ),
}
